# Wave I.3 — `guard:thin-shell`

## Problem

I.1 / I.2 removed static Urban owner-panel and starter product imports from the operator shell. Without a **machine-checked** rule, the next PR can reintroduce `@app-tour/workspace-denali|urban|…` into `apps/web` routes and wipe that progress.

Hostile audit: thin shell ~35% — directory cleanup is not enough; the **import graph** must stay thin.

## Decision

Add `pnpm run guard:thin-shell` (`scripts/guards/guard-thin-shell.mjs`):

**Scope:** `apps/web/src/**`, `apps/web/app/**` (`.ts` / `.tsx` / `.js` / `.mjs`).

**Forbidden:** any `@app-tour/workspace-*` **except** `@app-tour/workspace-sdk` (static `from` / `import()` / type-only).

**Allowlist (temporary until later Waves):**

| Path | Why |
| ---- | --- |
| `**/*.generated.*` | Manifest codegen loaders (dynamic `import()` of products) |
| `apps/web/src/workspace-theme-css.d.ts` | Ambient CSS module declarations only |

~~`wizard/denali/**`~~ — **removed in Wave I.4** ([`wave-i-4-denali-adapters-codegen.mdoc`](./wave-i-4-denali-adapters-codegen.mdoc)): firewall path stays for stable imports, but must not contain product package imports.

Wire into [`wave-i0:guard`](./wave-i-0-architecture-guard-matrix.mdoc) so the architecture matrix fails closed.

## Out of scope

- Shrinking or deleting `wizard/denali/*` (Wave I.4+)
- Removing product packages from `apps/web/package.json`
- Scanning `apps/web/test/**` (tests may still import products)

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run guard:thin-shell
pnpm run wave-i0:guard
# expect PASS
```
